diff --git a/inputstream.adaptive/changelog.txt b/inputstream.adaptive/changelog.txt
index 4fcc1c4..6b96a34 100644
--- a/inputstream.adaptive/changelog.txt
+++ b/inputstream.adaptive/changelog.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@ v21.5.25-p3i.4 (2026-10-31)
 - Fix a change of the stream quality that could start before the reader of the old quality returned all frames, while a read of the next frame was still in progress
 - Fix a seek during a change of the stream quality: a seek into the segment of the change read data of the new quality into the reader of the old quality, and a seek to the first segment continued at the segment of the change
 - Fix a possible crash at a change of the stream quality: the reopen of the stream allocated more segment buffers while a download used the buffers
+- Fix a seek during a change of the stream quality, which continued at the start of the segment instead of at the seek time
+- Fix wrong stream times, a wrong seek limit of a live stream and seeks to the wrong segment with a high timescale or large times (for example times from 1970 at 90 kHz), where a time conversion overflowed
+- Fix a DASH SegmentList without a timescale, whose segment times counted in microseconds instead of seconds
 - Fix a seek to an earlier time inside the current segment, which continued at the start of the segment instead of at the frame of the seek time
 - Fix a seek in a TS stream with video and audio that returned an audio frame first, so the other streams aligned to the audio time instead of the video frame of the seek
 - Fix a seek in an HEVC or MPEG-2 TS stream, which continued at the segment start instead of at the key frame of the seek time
